I (4034) board: ########################################################################
Listener voice keyboard firmware usage:
Board profile: Voice Keyboard V2, ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8, 16MB flash, 8MB Octal PSRAM.
Inject test bytes with tools/send_serial.ps1 or type in monitor.
Capture 3s audio WAV with tools/capture_audio_wav.ps1 -Port COM3.
Capture toggle session WAV with tools/capture_audio_session_wav.ps1 -Port COM3.
EC11 push/GPIO18 is the physical power-on key; after boot, single click sends the EC11 custom-key fallback Shift+F13 after the 200 ms double-click window.
EC11 push fast double-click clears BLE pairing/session state when no recording is active; long press stays reserved for hardware power control.
Logical custom keys: single-click KEY1-KEY4 fallback=F13-F16, double-click=F17-F20, long-press=F21-F24.
KEY1/GPIO38, KEY2/GPIO39, KEY3/GPIO40, KEY4/GPIO41 send safe non-text BLE HID usages while Listener-Type custom actions are unavailable; recording is a configurable custom-key action.
Generated button diagnostics: ~KEY:KEY3:SINGLE simulates the recording custom-key path for automated A1/A2 tests; ~KEY:EC11:SINGLE simulates the EC11 runtime custom-key press/release path.
Send ~VREC:RECOVERY to clear pairing/session state over USB.
Board diagnostics: ~BOARD:STATUS reports V2 pin, USB, charger, battery, PWR_HOLD/GPIO9, mic, reserved MSPI, and LED resource status; ~BOARD:POWER reports optional current rails as not_populated on the current board.
Board USB_DET diagnostics: GPIO7 USB_DET is disabled/high-Z; computer USB is inferred from USB Serial/JTAG SOF and charger state from BAT_CHG/BAT_STD; ~BOARD:USB_DET:HIGHZ reports the disabled state.
Board GPIO diagnostics: ~BOARD:GPIO reads raw KEY1-KEY4 and EC11 A/B/key levels without reconfiguring pins.
Board GPIO scan: ~BOARD:GPIO-SCAN samples all valid GPIO levels without reconfiguring pins and prints changed GPIOs.
Board PWR_HOLD diagnostics: ~BOARD:PWR-HOLD:LOW restores runtime low; ~BOARD:PWR-HOLD:HIGH attempts the shutdown high drive and may power off the board.
Input flash debug: ~DIAGLOG:INPUTDBG:ON records high-volume key/EC11 debug events until ~DIAGLOG:INPUTDBG:OFF or reboot.
Power diagnostics: ~POWER:STATUS reports state/blockers/battery/power-hold status; ~POWER:PM reports ESP PM locks; ~POWER:SHUTDOWN or ~POWER:TEST:SHUTDOWN requests manual hardware shutdown.
Device settings: ~DEVICE:SETTINGS reports user device config; ~DEVICE:SET plugged_brightness=80 battery_brightness=50 low_power_idle_minutes=1 plugged_low_power_enabled=0 auto_shutdown_minutes=off ble_name=listener updates persisted settings.
LED diagnostics: ~LED:STATUS reports four WS2812 groups; ~LED:TEST:RGBW and ~LED:TEST:MAP stay brightness-gated until VDD_LED sign-off.
Watchdog diagnostics: ~WDT:STATUS reports config, ~WDT:DEADLOCK intentionally triggers Task WDT reset.
Boot safety diagnostics: ~BOOT:STATUS reports crash counter, ~BOOT:CRASH restarts for validation, ~BOOT:CLEAR clears safe mode.
Use ~OTA:STATUS, ~OTA:BLOCKER, or ~OTA:ABORT for firmware OTA diagnostics.
Use ~DIAGLOG:COUNT, ~DIAGLOG:LAST:N, ~DIAGLOG:DUMP, or ~DIAGLOG:CLEAR for diagnostics.
Device status logs use ready, recording, transferring, error, and recovery.
End-to-end keystroke delivery still requires a BLE host connection.
